 3. 🇮🇷 Trump expects Iran negotiations this week 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump, honorary chair of the Presidents Cup golf tournament, cheers on the first tee while attending the final round yesterday at Medinah Country Club in suburban Chicago. Photo: Luke Hales/Getty Images The day after rejecting an Iranian proposal to end the war, President Trump told Axios' Barak Ravid in a phone interview that U.S. negotiators will engage in more talks with the country this week: 

 Qatar and other regional mediators are trying to revive negotiations between the U.S. and Iran, but the two sides are far apart on the key issues, Barak writes .

 While Iran wants to focus any talks on the Strait of Hormuz and the U.S. naval blockade, the Trump administration is demanding that Iran agree to nuclear concessions. "I expect more talks with Iran [this week]," Trump said. "They want to make a deal, but it is not the deal that I want to make. It is what we would have maybe agreed to a year ago. They overplayed their hand."

 Asked if he is considering resuming strikes against Iran, Trump said: "I am always thinking about it." Keep reading . 

 
 
