 6. 💰 Exclusive: Data-center backers plan for &#x27;27 and beyond 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Photo: Brandon Bell/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 AI companies, private equity firms and unions are banding together to form a new multimillion-dollar coalition to make the case for responsible growth in seven key states, Axios' Hans Nichols reports. 

 Why it matters: The new group, the American Infrastructure Alliance , wants to partner with state and local officials to create clear standards and guardrails for data centers in 2027. In return, the coalition hopes to head off any moratoriums on new construction. The group plans initial campaigns in Texas, Georgia, Ohio, Iowa, Pennsylvania, Indiana and South Carolina.

 The alliance is backed by Blackstone, OpenAI, QTS and SoftBank Group, along with key unions, including the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers (IBEW). 🔭 Between the lines: The group represents an initial investment in a broader battle over AI and data centers that will likely bleed into the 2027 state legislative battles and the 2028 presidential campaign.

